<body>
    <h1>Download files or photo in react native</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>Update:</p>
<p>20230504 Because of the bug on <code>rn-fetch-blob</code>, so we change =
to use <code>expo-file-system</code> to download the file. But the flow is =
still the same.</p>
<p></p>
<p>Use <code>rn-fetch-blob</code> library to download file or image</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Install the <code>rn-fetch-blob</code> library by running the following =
command in your terminal:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">npm ins=
tall rn-fetch-blob --save</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p>Import the <code>RNFetchBlob</code> module from <code>rn-fetch-blob</cod=
e> at the top of your component file:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">import =
RNFetchBlob from 'rn-fetch-blob'</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
</ol>
<h2 id=3D"Downloadfilesorphotoinreactnative-Image">Image</h2>
<p>You can save images to the device's camera roll using the <code>react-na=
tive-camera-roll</code> library. Here are the steps to download and save an=
 image from a URL to the camera roll:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Install the <code>react-native-camera-roll</code> library by running the=
 following command in your terminal:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">npm ins=
tall react-native-camera-roll --save</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p>Import the <code>CameraRoll</code> module from <code>react-native-camera=
-roll</code> at the top of your component file:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">import =
CameraRoll from 'react-native-camera-roll'</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p>Use the <code>rn-fetch-blob</code> API to download the image from the UR=
L:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">const d=
ownloadImage =3D async(url) =3D&gt; {
  await RNFetchBlob.config({
    fileCache: true,
  }).fetch('GET', url)
  return fileDir
}</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p>Use the <code>CameraRoll.saveToCameraRoll</code> method to save the imag=
e to the device's camera roll:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">const s=
aveImageToCameraRoll =3D async(fileDir) =3D&gt; {
  CameraRoll.saveToCameraRoll(fileDir, 'photo')
    .then(() =3D&gt; {
      // Code to display a success message
    })
    .catch((error) =3D&gt; {
      // Code to display an error message
    });
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>In the above example, the <code>CameraRoll.saveToCameraRoll</code> metho=
d is used to save the <code>fileDir</code> as a photo to the device's camer=
a roll. The method returns a Promise that resolves when the save is success=
ful and rejects when it fails.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Call the <code>downloadImage</code> and <code>saveImageToCameraRoll</cod=
e> functions when the user wants to download and save the image, such as wh=
en they tap a button:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">const h=
andleDownloadButtonPress =3D async () =3D&gt; {
  const fileDir =3D await downloadImage('https://example.com/image.jpg')
  await saveImageToCameraRoll(fileDir)
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>In the above example, the <code>downloadImage</code> function is called =
with the URL of the image to download, and the <code>saveImageToCameraRoll<=
/code> function is called with the <code>fileDir</code> representing the do=
wnloaded image.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 id=3D"Downloadfilesorphotoinreactnative-File">File</h2>
<p>Here are the steps to download a file from a URL to the device's externa=
l storage:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Use the <code>RNFetchBlob.config</code> method to configure the download=
 request and the <code>fetch</code> API to download the file from the URL:<=
/p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">const d=
ownloadFile =3D async (url, fileName) =3D&gt; {
  const { dirs } =3D RNFetchBlob.fs;
  const fileDir =3D `${dirs.DownloadDir}/${fileName}`;
 =20
  await RNFetchBlob.config({
    fileCache: true,
    path: fileDir,
  }).fetch('GET', url);
 =20
  return fileDir;
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>In the above example, the <code>RNFetchBlob.config</code> method is used=
 to configure the download request with the <code>fileCache</code> and <cod=
e>path</code> options. The <code>fileCache</code> option enables file cachi=
ng for the download request, and the <code>path</code> option specifies the=
 path of the downloaded file. The <code>fetch</code> API is then used to do=
wnload the file from the specified URL.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Call the <code>downloadFile</code> function when the user wants to downl=
oad the file, such as when they tap a button:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">const h=
andleDownloadButtonPress =3D async () =3D&gt; {
  const fileDir =3D await downloadFile('https://example.com/file.pdf', 'myf=
ile.pdf');
  // Code to display a success message or open the downloaded file
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>In the above example, the <code>downloadFile</code> function is called w=
ith the URL of the file to download and the desired file name. The function=
 returns the path of the downloaded file in the device's external storage.<=
/p></li>
</ol>
<p>Note that this approach saves the file to the device's external storage,=
 which requires the <code>WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE</code> permission on Andro=
id. On iOS, the file is saved to the app's sandboxed storage by default. If=
 you want to save the file to a custom directory outside the app's sandbox,=
 you can use a file picker library to prompt the user to choose a directory=
 and save the file there. However, this requires user interaction and is su=
bject to the limitations of the iOS sandboxing system.</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
